{#
compose/_send_toast.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The dock's "Sending… — Undo" toast.

`hide_after` is ComposeController::CANCEL_WINDOW_MS rather than a literal, and
that matters: this toast's lifetime IS the cancel window, because the Undo link
goes when the toast goes. It used to be a bare 8000 here while the inline
reply bar counted 10000, both undocumented, and the difference was the bug —
the inline surface offered a cancel right up to the instant the worker claimed
the message, so a late click was confirmed and the mail went anyway. Both
surfaces now take the number from the controller, and the controller keeps it
below the send delay.

Variables: message, cancelWindow
#}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            type: 'success',
            message: 'compose.sending'|trans,
            extra: {
                undo_url: path('app_compose_mail_undo', { id: message.id }),
                hide_after: cancelWindow
            }
        } %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

<turbo-stream action="update" target="compose_dock">
    <template></template>
</turbo-stream>
